sections.content:
When something goes wrong, you have choices:

**Return codes** - Error-prone, easy to ignore:
```bpl
local result: int = divide(10, 0);  # Returns -1 for error?
# Easy to forget to check!
```

**Exceptions** - Explicit, can't be ignored:
```bpl
try {
    local result: int = divide(10, 0);  # Throws!
} catch (e: DivisionError) {
    printf("Error: %s\n", e.message);
}
```

Exceptions separate error handling from normal flow.

languages.BPL:
try {
    throw MyError { msg: "oops" };
} catch (e: MyError) {
    printf("%s", e.msg);
}

languages.C++:
try {
    throw MyError("oops");
} catch (MyError& e) {
    cout << e.what();
}

languages.Python:
try:
    raise MyError("oops")
except MyError as e:
    print(e)

languages.JavaScript:
try {
    throw new MyError("oops");
} catch (e) {
    console.log(e);
}

